Their ISS-097 stands regardless and is the useful half: a reader must search root AND every
  worktree per slug, then take max cycle across copies. Told them to record that the ROOT copy is
  authoritative and a worktree copy is a stale duplicate, so the fix does not treat them as peers.
  That is the THIRD reader defect today from the same unmodelled multi-worktree shape, written by
  the session that had just fixed the first two.

ISS-052 sent back to Umesh rather than closed, and the reasoning is stronger than security:
  plan.md:224 ends Phase 1 with a 5-counsellor pilot and plan.md:230 makes the P1 exit gate
  "post-session notes approved with light edits >=80%". Approving notes IS that screen, so it is
  the instrument one of the four P1 exit criteria is COMPUTED FROM, by five real counsellors, with
  no identity -- the >=80% is unattributable, the gate cannot be audited, a disputed approval has
  no owner. Measurement integrity, not just access control. It also resolves the decision-5 vs
  decision-6 tension in one direction: the plan says the counsellor is present AND approving, so
  counsellor-present is confirmed and nobody-opens-the-screen is contradicted.

docs/spec.md DOES NOT EXIST -- the PLAN gate substitutes qa/contracts/counselling-engine.md, a
  deliberate recorded substitution, but the maker skill's step 5bb cites "the flows in
  docs/spec.md". Any persona-walk brief must name the substitution explicitly rather than let a
  walker discover an empty path. Recorded here for whoever writes the B17/B19 persona units.

Umesh now has SIX items, not five: the three relayed-unconfirmed gates, the two unanswered gates
